WEBVTT

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:02.610
What? Support staff are on the course?

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:04.040
Huh? Kyoto?

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:04.940
But why?

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:07.770
Did they get them mixed up
 with Hakone Academy?

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:11.610
You were in the same position as Sohoku.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:14.530
You didn't hear the correction on the radio?

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:18.120
They shook off the others.

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:20.800
B-By himself?

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:25.960
This year there are two 
of them chasing the leaders!

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:27.850
Two times one is two.

00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:29.710
Two times two is four.

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:31.520
Two times three is six.

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:33.130
Two times four is eight.

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:34.800
Two times five is ten.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.590
Two times six is 12.

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:38.430
Two times seven is 14.

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:40.440
Two times eight is 16.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.500
Two times nine is 18.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.290
They're teeming with muscles!

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:47.730
Mi...

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:49.320
Midousuji...

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:52.690
We caught up!

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:01.700
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:03.790
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:32.590
<i>LINE.03 The Appointed Time</i>

00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:32.120
<i>There are 3.5 kilometers to 
the first day's finish line.</i>

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:33.960
<i>And he caught up now?</i>

00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:37.800
Seriously?

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:38.510
Whoa!

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:41.090
I found you!

00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:42.930
<i>They've been coming after us?</i>

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:45.180
<i>They passed Aoyagi-san,
Kaburagi, and the others?</i>

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.270
<i>Kyoto Fushimi?</i>

00:02:47.270 --> 00:02:49.440
<i>I heard they disrupted the race last year.</i>

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:53.020
<i>It must be all the pressure he's 
exerting that makes him look huge.</i>

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:58.090
<i>I can tell. He's calculated everything.</i>

00:02:58.090 --> 00:03:00.360
<i>He is only thinking about winning.</i>

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:07.080
<i>Kyoto Fushimi's Midousuji...</i>

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:09.120
<i>You're exactly as Fukutomi-san 
described last year.</i>

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:14.750
Though we lost the overall race, 
this year's power rankings

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:20.550
put Hakone Academy first, 
Sohoku next, and then the rest.

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:21.590
Yes, sir.

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:24.680
But Kyoto Fushimi's Midousuji...

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:29.550
This loss will push him to 
enter the Inter-High again.

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:36.180
Kuroda, unless your resolve is strong 
by the time you become a third-year,

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:38.070
Hakone Academy won't reclaim its throne.

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:38.990
Yes, sir.

00:03:38.990 --> 00:03:41.730
After all, there will be three!

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:44.170
Hakone Academy, Sohoku, and Kyoto Fushimi!

00:03:44.170 --> 00:03:45.780
It will be an era of three powerhouses!

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:50.450
Three powerhouses...

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:53.500
What are you looking at, Hakone Academy?

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:59.300
Were you lost in thought 
in the middle of a race?

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:01.260
<i>It took him a second to come up on my left.</i>

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:02.760
<i>He's fast.</i>

00:04:03.130 --> 00:04:05.680
<i>But I just have to do 
everything I can to stop him.</i>

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:08.600
Wow!

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:09.640
Huh?

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:18.020
What?!

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:20.230
What are you doing?

00:04:21.220 --> 00:04:22.600
I'm sorry.

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:25.990
As a first-year, this is my first Inter-High.

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:31.250
I was so happy to see one of the rumored 
Hakone Academy riders that I stumbled.

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:33.370
So happy you stumbled?

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:35.160
<i>Nice muscles.</i>

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:38.860
<i>So these are the rumored cat legs
 of Hakone Academy's Kuroda.</i>

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:41.240
<i>I couldn't help but touch them...</i>

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:42.700
<i>And make a sound, too.</i>

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:46.180
<i>There are so many wonderful muscles right 
before the finish line at the Inter-High!</i>

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:50.060
<i>That's #116, Kishigami Komari.</i>

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:52.640
<i>He did something similar to me
 before the race started.</i>

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:55.520
<i>Is he trying to agitate us?</i>

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:57.400
<i>What's his deal?</i>

00:04:57.770 --> 00:04:58.650
Muscles...

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:00.890
<i>He was listed as a substitute.</i>

00:05:00.890 --> 00:05:04.030
<i>So why is he here before the finish line?</i>

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:07.030
<i>In any case, right now,
 I should focus on the finish line.</i>

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:09.210
<i>Don't let them manipulate you.</i>

00:05:09.210 --> 00:05:13.130
<i>On this year's first day, 
after we pass Lake Chuzenji,</i>

00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:18.210
<i>the elevation rapidly rises toward the 
finish line in a winding uphill climb.</i>

00:05:20.330 --> 00:05:21.460
Wait! Where is he?

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:22.380
<i>He's gone!</i>

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:24.760
<i>Where is Midousuji?</i>

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:26.650
Midousuji's gone!

00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:27.850
Yuki-chan!

00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:31.930
Did he take advantage of the 
confusion caused by #116...

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:34.060
And attack?

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:36.350
He's above us!

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:38.190
He's going for the solo finish!

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:40.190
Faster, Naruko!

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:41.940
We can't leave him
 for the last three kilometers!

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:46.240
Damn! How does Midousuji get me every time?

00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:47.260
Naruko?

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:51.690
<i>What's going on? Why isn't he here?</i>

00:05:51.690 --> 00:05:53.290
Naruko!

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:57.250
<i>I caught up, caused a commotion, 
and took advantage of it to attack.</i>

00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:59.750
<i>Just as planned.</i>

00:06:00.170 --> 00:06:02.930
<i>All I want is victory.</i>

00:06:02.930 --> 00:06:05.460
<i>All I need is victory.</i>

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:08.470
<i>I'll leave them in the dust.</i>

00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:14.970
And Komari-kun really does 
have no self control.

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:17.390
<i>Just three kilometers left.</i>

00:06:17.390 --> 00:06:20.770
<i>I'll take the finish line alone.</i>

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:22.490
Kyoto Fushimi's in the lead!

00:06:22.490 --> 00:06:24.020
Wow, seriously?

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:29.280
Kyoto Fushimi's #111, Midousuji, 
is the first to come up the hill!

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:32.280
<i>At least, I was supposed to.</i>

00:06:32.890 --> 00:06:34.030
And behind him is...

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:39.610
<i>But you're the only one who 
didn't take his eyes off me...</i>

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:43.750
<i>You chicken-headed bean!</i>

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:46.250
You should be thanking me, Midousuji.

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:50.010
I thought you'd be bored traveling alone,
 so I tagged along.

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:52.560
Sohoku's in second! It's Naruko!

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:54.760
He's keeping up with Midousuji by himself!

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:56.290
What's going on?

00:06:56.290 --> 00:06:59.970
Ten minutes ago, they reported that Sohoku 
and Hakone Academy were racing for first!

00:06:59.970 --> 00:07:01.330
I don't see the others!

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:02.680
There's three kilometers left!

00:07:02.680 --> 00:07:04.440
What's going to happen?

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:07.410
This is the best part of road racing!

00:07:07.410 --> 00:07:10.700
There's no telling who 
will take the finish line!

00:07:11.010 --> 00:07:16.030
I hope you haven't forgotten 
last winter's battle, Midousuji!

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:20.860
Did something happen?

00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:23.540
The seasons have changed.

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:26.070
<i>Chicken-headed bean...</i>

00:07:26.070 --> 00:07:31.140
<i>It was impressive enough that you were 
the only one not to take his eyes off me,</i>

00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:33.390
<i>but what really deserves recognition...</i>

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:39.180
<i>is that you kept up with 
my attack on the climb.</i>

00:07:39.530 --> 00:07:42.600
<i>You were supposed to be a sprinter.</i>

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:46.400
<i>You even abandoned the deep 
wheels you were so proud of.</i>

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:53.070
<i>This man really did quit being a 
sprinter to become an all-rounder!</i>

00:07:54.310 --> 00:07:58.950
Sorry. I can't remember, chicken-headed bean.

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:02.120
I can see in your eyes 
that you do, Midousuji!

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:04.210
A sprinter...

00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:12.760
I don't mind a man so 
willing to give that up.

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:16.970
You idiot! I'm here to reclaim that!

00:08:17.410 --> 00:08:23.440
Here? With less than three kilometers 
to the finish line at the Inter-High?

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:28.320
Your plan is to race against me 
and reclaim the title of sprinter?

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:30.570
What could be more tense, right?

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:36.930
Fine. Sounds interesting.

00:08:36.930 --> 00:08:39.660
I'll do it. But...

00:08:43.220 --> 00:08:46.530
Only if you can catch up to me!

00:08:46.530 --> 00:08:49.080
Kyoto Fushimi's accelerating 
on the winding uphill!

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:50.150
What is that?

00:08:50.150 --> 00:08:52.160
He leans so far forward when he dances!

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:52.970
He's so fast!

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:54.820
He's still accelerating!

00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:59.430
<i>You may have gotten faster on the climb, 
but you're still only a sprinter.</i>

00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:04.770
<i>You can't catch up to me with 
just a little bit of effort.</i>

00:09:08.260 --> 00:09:09.170
Huh?

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:15.280
Sohoku's Naruko is keeping up with 
Kyoto Fushimi's acceleration!

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:18.280
Incredible! That red-headed guy's so fast,
 even though he's small!

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:21.240
Don't think you can pull 
ahead of me on the climb!

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:23.790
I told you so before we started, Midousuji!

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:28.250
I'm all about experiencing 
things to understand them.

00:09:28.850 --> 00:09:31.130
Not bad, chicken-head.

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:33.610
Rather, Naruko-kun.

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:39.430
Shall we work together until 
the finish line, then?

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:43.110
Good idea, right?

00:09:43.110 --> 00:09:47.100
You and I are the only ones nearing 
the finish line right now.

00:09:47.450 --> 00:09:52.290
If we work together, we'll arrive 
at the finish line first.

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:55.110
Even you could take it first.

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:59.360
You'll be able to deliver your 
precious jersey to the finish line.

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:01.910
Oh, it's okay.

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:05.510
Don't worry. I'm talking 
about peaceful cooperation.

00:10:05.510 --> 00:10:09.980
I just want to finish as highly ranked 
as possible today for tomorrow.

00:10:09.980 --> 00:10:17.800
If you pedal really hard, then as a symbol 
of our friendship, I'll let you—

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:19.400
You're bluffing.

00:10:19.400 --> 00:10:22.050
Those aren't the eyes of a 
man willing to give that up.

00:10:23.350 --> 00:10:24.680
I'm bluffing!

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:27.830
Don't use words like "friendship" that 
aren't part of your normal vocabulary!

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:33.980
<i>He shifted up.</i>

00:10:37.990 --> 00:10:39.030
<i>This guy...</i>

00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:42.200
<i>He's stronger than he was last winter!</i>

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:45.400
<i>That massive pressure was real!</i>

00:10:45.400 --> 00:10:47.000
Oh, right.

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:52.790
Chicken-head, as a special treat, 
I'll show you something.

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:57.210
I still have something special up my sleeve.

00:11:02.810 --> 00:11:04.850
Where are we, Tadokorocchi?

00:11:06.570 --> 00:11:10.590
Kanzaki-san told me there's a traffic jam.

00:11:10.590 --> 00:11:11.310
This is a shortcut.

00:11:11.310 --> 00:11:14.520
I know you're the
 Rampaging Human Bullet, but...

00:11:16.920 --> 00:11:18.780
You have to have limits, Tadokoro!

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:20.920
You can count on me.

00:11:20.920 --> 00:11:23.300
We'll make it in time to 
see the end of the race!

00:11:26.010 --> 00:11:26.850
Yuki-chan!

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:28.900
I know! He got past us!

00:11:29.560 --> 00:11:32.120
Did Naruko go after Midousuji?

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:34.250
We'll go after them at full speed, Ashikiba!

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:35.210
Yeah!

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:38.000
<i>There's no point if we can't catch up.</i>

00:11:38.360 --> 00:11:42.930
<i>Hakone Academy has to be part 
of the race for the finish line!</i>

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:46.920
Sohoku's Imaizumi!

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:50.100
Shall we work together?

00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:53.940
Don't you want to stop Midousuji?

00:11:54.420 --> 00:11:56.110
We'll cooperate until then.

00:11:58.280 --> 00:12:01.620
<i>Cooperate with Hakone Academy?</i>

00:12:01.620 --> 00:12:03.550
<i>There are three kilometers to the finish line.</i>

00:12:03.550 --> 00:12:06.360
<i>Hakone Academy is an opposing 
team racing for the finish line.</i>

00:12:06.810 --> 00:12:09.160
<i>But Midousuji is in front of me.</i>

00:12:09.690 --> 00:12:10.410
I'm in!

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:12.370
I'll cooperate with you, Kuroda-san!

00:12:12.690 --> 00:12:17.250
Good, but only if you can 
keep up with my top speed!

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:18.970
I'm flipping my switch!

00:12:21.780 --> 00:12:24.670
Don't get left behind, Imaizumi!

00:12:24.670 --> 00:12:25.260
Got it!

00:12:26.130 --> 00:12:28.870
Sohoku and Hakone Academy 
are climbing together!

00:12:28.870 --> 00:12:30.630
Wow, they're cooperating!

00:12:30.630 --> 00:12:32.640
And Kuroda's a fast climber!

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:33.910
Of course he is!

00:12:33.910 --> 00:12:35.900
He used to be one!

00:12:36.950 --> 00:12:37.860
<i>Incredible...</i>

00:12:38.180 --> 00:12:41.070
<i>He's pulling me upward as we accelerate,
 even on this incline.</i>

00:12:41.070 --> 00:12:43.100
Don't underestimate me, Kyoto Fushimi!

00:12:43.100 --> 00:12:47.700
I'll make you regret 
challenging me on a climb!

00:12:49.240 --> 00:12:51.670
<i>This is different from how 
he was racing earlier.</i>

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:53.270
<i>Did he do something?</i>

00:12:53.270 --> 00:12:55.570
<i>His pressure has increased.</i>

00:12:55.570 --> 00:12:57.580
<i>He said something about a switch earlier.</i>

00:12:58.060 --> 00:13:02.130
<i>Does this have something to do 
with him touching his temple?</i>

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:04.720
<i>Yuki-chan...</i>

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:06.990
<i>You flipped your switch.</i>

00:13:06.990 --> 00:13:10.260
<i>You're always so fast when you do.</i>

00:13:10.660 --> 00:13:13.390
Huh? What's my switch?

00:13:13.790 --> 00:13:16.320
You always get faster before 
the finish line when

00:13:16.320 --> 00:13:19.200
you say you're flipping your switch.

00:13:19.200 --> 00:13:21.320
I was wondering what kind of 
magical incantation it is.

00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:21.940
What?

00:13:21.940 --> 00:13:23.720
It's not an incantation.

00:13:23.720 --> 00:13:25.830
What are you, a high school girl
 who believes in jinxes?

00:13:26.630 --> 00:13:30.080
I have a scar right here.

00:13:30.420 --> 00:13:31.700
Really?

00:13:32.130 --> 00:13:34.440
I guess you hadn't heard.

00:13:34.440 --> 00:13:37.960
A long time ago, I once suffered 
an injury related to my pride.

00:13:38.530 --> 00:13:45.420
When I turn on my switch, I'm scraping 
off the unhealed scab with my nail.

00:13:46.340 --> 00:13:49.030
That's what you've been doing, Yuki-chan?

00:13:49.030 --> 00:13:51.390
It bleeds nicely when I do.

00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:53.100
It clears my mind.

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:55.940
It revives the old me.

00:13:56.740 --> 00:14:01.690
The man who couldn't stand 
not being best at everything.

00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:03.610
And then...

00:14:03.950 --> 00:14:07.280
<i>It heightens my competitiveness, my focus.</i>

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:10.180
<i>My desire to consume my enemies shoots up.</i>

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:11.480
Kyoto Fushimi!

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:14.910
<i>I can feel it, Yuki-chan.</i>

00:14:14.910 --> 00:14:16.120
<i>I feel it.</i>

00:14:17.110 --> 00:14:18.420
<i>It's heightened for me, too!</i>

00:14:20.930 --> 00:14:23.300
<i>Ashikiba-san increased his pressure, too?</i>

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:29.930
<i>Does working together do that for this 
year's #1 and #2 from Hakone Academy?</i>

00:14:30.360 --> 00:14:33.260
<i>Was agreeing to cooperate 
with them a mistake?</i>

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:37.270
<b>Kuroda</b>

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:37.270
<b>Imaizumi</b>

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:37.270
<b>Ashikiba</b>

00:14:33.830 --> 00:14:37.270
<i>I'm helping my opponents 
get to the finish line.</i>

00:14:33.990 --> 00:14:37.270
<b>Midousuji</b>

00:14:33.990 --> 00:14:37.270
<b>Naruko</b>

00:14:37.590 --> 00:14:40.290
<i>Sohoku has Naruko nearing the finish line.</i>

00:14:40.290 --> 00:14:43.190
<i>Should I have tried to stop 
Hakone Academy instead?</i>

00:14:44.520 --> 00:14:45.440
<i>No.</i>

00:14:46.100 --> 00:14:50.130
<i>They could reach the front 
without my cooperation.</i>

00:14:50.130 --> 00:14:52.980
<i>And if that happened, Sohoku would be alone.</i>

00:14:52.980 --> 00:14:54.620
<i>We'd be at an overwhelming disadvantage.</i>

00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:57.800
Wow, Sohoku's pulling for Hakone Academy!

00:14:57.800 --> 00:15:01.510
Last year's rival teams are working 
together to pursue the leaders!

00:15:01.510 --> 00:15:02.400
Such passion!

00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:03.880
Take a picture!

00:15:04.230 --> 00:15:07.800
Not bad, Imaizumi. You pull well.

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:09.470
It's smooth and efficient.

00:15:09.840 --> 00:15:12.990
And you're smart. I know what you're thinking.

00:15:12.990 --> 00:15:16.370
You're wondering if you made the right 
choice by agreeing to cooperate.

00:15:17.320 --> 00:15:18.600
I like that look in your eyes.

00:15:20.330 --> 00:15:23.980
They're the eyes of a lively and proud elite.

00:15:27.220 --> 00:15:29.380
I can tell from your face 
that you don't think I understand.

00:15:29.380 --> 00:15:31.380
Sorry, but I do. I get it.

00:15:31.380 --> 00:15:33.300
After all, I used to be an elite.

00:15:33.300 --> 00:15:37.120
You don't go with the crowd, you don't 
back down, and you don't listen to others.

00:15:37.460 --> 00:15:40.160
<i>Kuroda-san's going even faster.</i>

00:15:40.670 --> 00:15:43.290
And yet you're still better than the rest.

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:44.790
No wonder you're confused.

00:15:45.270 --> 00:15:47.850
I'm not like that.

00:15:47.850 --> 00:15:50.090
Good luck with that, kid.

00:15:51.770 --> 00:15:53.940
I've worked harder than anyone else.

00:15:53.940 --> 00:15:55.010
That's why I'm strong.

00:15:55.010 --> 00:15:56.340
I've achieved things, too.

00:15:56.340 --> 00:15:58.890
It has nothing to do with being an elite.

00:15:59.990 --> 00:16:05.270
In order to become stronger 
and rise higher...

00:16:07.490 --> 00:16:10.780
Have you ever bowed your head 
to the one you hate the most?

00:16:15.080 --> 00:16:17.770
That's it. Keep it up, Imaizumi.

00:16:17.770 --> 00:16:20.790
I'd like to see how far your 
friendly little club gets you.

00:16:21.970 --> 00:16:25.890
I believe a team is about becoming 
stronger by struggling against

00:16:26.310 --> 00:16:28.800
and hating each other.

00:16:29.140 --> 00:16:31.160
Well, good luck.

00:16:32.280 --> 00:16:35.300
Yuki-chan, I'll switch 
with you. I'll lead next.

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:36.680
Stay back, Takuto!

00:16:39.110 --> 00:16:42.020
But we need to catch up 
as quickly as possible.

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:44.350
And all three of us are working together.

00:16:44.750 --> 00:16:46.250
Don't be absurd, Takuto!

00:16:46.250 --> 00:16:47.850
You're the ace!

00:16:47.850 --> 00:16:51.030
Taking the finish line is the ace's job!

00:16:52.040 --> 00:16:54.840
Trusting your assistants and 
conserving your strength

00:16:54.840 --> 00:16:57.410
no matter how bad it gets is your job!

00:16:58.210 --> 00:16:59.820
Don't worry.

00:16:59.820 --> 00:17:01.950
I'll pull twice as hard for you.

00:17:02.370 --> 00:17:05.620
And if Imaizumi's not happy with that,
 I'll pull three times as hard.

00:17:06.100 --> 00:17:10.250
<i>Even under these circumstances, 
he still intends to be his assistant?</i>

00:17:10.630 --> 00:17:12.420
Just shut up and follow me.

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:15.050
I'm Black Cat Kuroda, the deliveryman!

00:17:20.390 --> 00:17:24.120
<i>But I still don't see Midousuji.</i>

00:17:24.120 --> 00:17:26.730
<i>Damn it. Only two 
and a half kilometers left.</i>

00:17:27.090 --> 00:17:29.340
<i>Will we fail to catch up to them?</i>

00:17:29.340 --> 00:17:30.610
<i>If that happens...</i>

00:17:31.190 --> 00:17:33.070
<i>I'm counting on you, Naruko!</i>

00:17:38.970 --> 00:17:41.500
You're at your limit.

00:17:41.500 --> 00:17:45.710
Is that the best you can do,
 chicken-headed bean?

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:50.210
In that case, the finish line is mine.

00:17:54.360 --> 00:17:57.240
There are 2.5 kilometers left to 
the first day's finish line!

00:17:57.240 --> 00:17:58.800
Kyoto Fushimi's in the lead!

00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:00.090
Go!

00:18:00.090 --> 00:18:01.300
Kyoto Fushimi!

00:18:01.830 --> 00:18:04.400
Kyoto Fushimi is amazing this year.

00:18:04.400 --> 00:18:07.420
I just heard over the radio that 
there's three guys chasing after them,

00:18:07.420 --> 00:18:09.480
but they're pretty far behind.

00:18:09.800 --> 00:18:15.240
He might actually be able to 
stay ahead of them and win!

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:17.490
Kyoto Fushimi's raising his pace!

00:18:17.490 --> 00:18:19.460
He's trying to stay ahead!

00:18:19.460 --> 00:18:21.170
Sohoku's desperately chasing after him!

00:18:21.170 --> 00:18:24.740
At this rate, the first day will go 
to either Sohoku or Kyoto Fushimi!

00:18:25.850 --> 00:18:29.920
<i>There are two ways to take the 
finish line in a road race.</i>

00:18:30.230 --> 00:18:34.200
<i>Either catch up to those who 
raced ahead for a "group finish,"</i>

00:18:34.200 --> 00:18:39.590
<i>or stay ahead of the others 
in a "running finish."</i>

00:18:39.920 --> 00:18:42.720
<i>I'm fairly far ahead of Hakone Academy.</i>

00:18:42.720 --> 00:18:46.840
<i>I read the terrain and timing 
to achieve this margin.</i>

00:18:46.840 --> 00:18:51.980
<i>If I can just maintain this lead, I'll win!</i>

00:18:53.080 --> 00:18:56.440
<i>Only two kilometers left!</i>

00:18:57.030 --> 00:19:00.450
<i>Winning, victory, the fruits of my labor...</i>

00:19:00.980 --> 00:19:03.410
<i>Proof I'm faster than the others.</i>

00:19:03.410 --> 00:19:05.700
<i>Stronger than the others.</i>

00:19:05.700 --> 00:19:08.370
<i>More right than the others.</i>

00:19:08.370 --> 00:19:11.090
<i>Purer than anything else.</i>

00:19:11.090 --> 00:19:13.790
<i>That is the finish line!</i>

00:19:14.190 --> 00:19:21.130
<i>So why are you trying so hard with 
clenched teeth and a pained expression?</i>

00:19:22.710 --> 00:19:27.640
Why? You should allow your spirit 
to be broken and just give up.

00:19:28.230 --> 00:19:32.400
Why are you so close, chicken-headed bean?

00:19:32.810 --> 00:19:35.460
What is it? The power of friendship?

00:19:35.460 --> 00:19:39.080
Is the energy Weakizumi-kun's 
sending you giving you courage?

00:19:39.080 --> 00:19:42.110
Don't push yourself so hard. 
Feel free to drop out.

00:19:42.560 --> 00:19:47.910
You said you'd race me if I caught up,
 so I caught up, Midousuji!

00:19:48.290 --> 00:19:51.770
I've been waiting for you to 
switch from watching your back

00:19:51.770 --> 00:19:56.880
to letting down your guard 
and only facing forward!

00:19:59.570 --> 00:20:02.130
You intend to get in my way?

00:20:02.460 --> 00:20:03.800
With all my might!

00:20:04.240 --> 00:20:07.060
What an unpleasant attitude.

00:20:07.460 --> 00:20:09.600
That's rich, coming from you.

00:20:10.600 --> 00:20:14.100
That's the perfect sound for a starting bell!

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:15.560
He's so fast!

00:20:15.560 --> 00:20:17.320
He was falling behind earlier!

00:20:17.320 --> 00:20:21.040
He let him get ahead so he could 
conserve his strength on the climb.

00:20:21.040 --> 00:20:22.570
What do you mean?

00:20:22.980 --> 00:20:24.870
The first day's course follows a

00:20:24.870 --> 00:20:28.420
winding road after Lake Chuzenji 
into the final uphill climb.

00:20:28.890 --> 00:20:30.790
Once you're through the birch forest,

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:36.250
it's a perfectly flat road at 
the base of Mount Nantaisan!

00:20:36.250 --> 00:20:40.090
Sohoku's #3 is a former sprinter!

00:20:42.340 --> 00:20:44.360
<i>A single road cutting through the trees.</i>

00:20:44.360 --> 00:20:46.890
<i>One thousand, seven hundred meters
 to the final finish line.</i>

00:20:46.890 --> 00:20:48.050
<i>Flat terrain.</i>

00:20:48.050 --> 00:20:49.430
<i>Just the two of us.</i>

00:20:49.970 --> 00:20:51.770
<i>It's just like that time!</i>

00:20:52.360 --> 00:20:53.690
<i>That time...</i>

00:20:54.210 --> 00:20:56.100
I'll quit sprinting!

00:20:56.490 --> 00:21:00.150
<i>It's just like our race in Osaka.</i>

00:21:00.520 --> 00:21:04.740
<i>And on top of that,
 we're racing for the finish line!</i>

00:21:05.380 --> 00:21:07.240
Surely you don't have any—

00:21:07.860 --> 00:21:13.080
No complaints here, chicken-headed bean.

00:21:14.620 --> 00:21:16.920
<i>He's breaking out his special technique.</i>

00:21:16.920 --> 00:21:23.720
I'll race you. However,
 you'll only get one chance.

00:21:24.420 --> 00:21:25.550
That's plenty.

00:21:29.260 --> 00:21:31.010
Gross!

00:21:31.450 --> 00:21:35.130
It's time for our race!

00:23:08.020 --> 00:23:13.160
Hello. Today I'd like to introduce 
you to Kyoto-style roast beef.

00:23:09.130 --> 00:23:13.160
<b>Kishigami Komari</b>

00:23:13.510 --> 00:23:15.490
<b>Kitchen</b>

00:23:16.020 --> 00:23:19.590
First you season it with 
salt and yuzu chili paste.

00:23:26.470 --> 00:23:29.240
<i>Good! This is good meat!</i>

00:23:29.240 --> 00:23:32.120
<i>The best meat!</i>

00:23:33.480 --> 00:23:36.330
You really are an impatient man.

00:23:36.330 --> 00:23:39.890
<i>NEXT RIDE Five Men's Resolve</i>

00:23:39.890 --> 00:23:44.900
This is a work of fiction. All characters and organizations
 appearing in this work are fictional. In this work,
 characters sometimes engage in dangerous activities.
 While riding bicycles on actual roads,
 please follow all traffic laws and ride safely.

00:23:44.900 --> 00:23:51.500
<b>Mura</b>
